  "note": "RBI, Outstanding liabilities of the Central Government (DBIE report 1399; Handbook of Statistics on the Indian Economy). Amounts in ₹ crore (DBIE serves rupees). External liabilities at the current exchange rate (Handbook note 2). Internal debt includes the Market Stabilisation Scheme from 2004-05 to 2012-13, and borrowing through extra-budgetary resources from 2016-17 (notes 4 and 5). The fall in 91-day bills in 1997-98 is the conversion of ad hoc Treasury bills into special securities (note 3). Stages, from the printed table's own note: accounts to 2024-25, the revised estimate for 2025-26 and the budget estimate for 2026-27, each in its own series (suffix __re and __be), never one line. Cross-checked against the printed table (Innovation Hub export of Handbook report 82): 470 of 470 figures match."
